 AIM
To write a C program to find the first palindromic string in an array of strings and analyze its time and space complexity.
ALGORITHM
1. Start.
2. Initialize an array of strings.
3. Traverse each string in the array.
4. Set left = 0 and right = length - 1.
5. Compare the characters at both pointers.
6. If they differ, the string is not a palindrome.
7. If they match, increment left and decrement right.
8. If the string is a palindrome, print it and stop.
9. If no palindrome is found, print an empty string.
10. Stop.
 PSEUDOCODE
Algorithm FirstPalindrome(words)
    for each word in words do
        left = 0
        right = length(word) - 1
        palindrome = TRUE

        while left < right do
            if word[left] != word[right] then
                palindrome = FALSE
                break
            end if
            left = left + 1
            right = right - 1
        end while

        if palindrome = TRUE then
            print word
            stop
        end if
    end for

    print ""
End Algorithm
SOURCE CODE (C)

#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

int main() {
    char words[5][20] = {
        "abc", "car", "ada", "racecar", "cool"
    };

    int i, left, right, palindrome;
    int found = 0;

    for (i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
        left = 0;
        right = strlen(words[i]) - 1;
        palindrome = 1;

        while (left < right) {
            if (words[i][left] != words[i][right]) {
                palindrome = 0;
                break;
            }

            left++;
            right--;
        }

        if (palindrome == 1) {
            printf("First Palindromic String: %s\n", words[i]);
            found = 1;
            break;
        }
    }

    if (found == 0) {
        printf("First Palindromic String: \"\"\n");
    }

    return 0;
}
INPUT
words = ["abc", "car", "ada", "racecar", "cool"]


OUTPUT
First Palindromic String: ada
Explanation: The strings "abc" and "car" are not palindromes. The string "ada" reads the same forward and backward, so it is the first palindrome.
7. COMPLEXITY ANALYSIS
Let:
- \(n\) = number of strings
- \(m\) = maximum length of a string
- Time Complexity: \(O(nm)\) — in the worst case, every string is checked.
- Auxiliary Space Complexity: \(O(1)\) — only a fixed number of variables are used.
8. RESULT
Thus, the C program successfully finds the first palindromic string in an array. The output is "ada", with worst-case time complexity \(O(nm)\) and auxiliary space complexity \(O(1)\).
